[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_pdjik")
fish_name = "Taiyaki Feeder"
grade = 1
sprite = ExtResource("2_7b31f")
catch_blurb = "Wait... it's alive???"
description = "Upon its first discovery, the Taiyaki Feeder was mistaken for a littered pastry that a previous fisher had thrown in the water. It was only until these fish started appearing more commonly throughout the waters that a further look was warranted. 

Turns out, their pastry-like design is nothing but a disguise for the fact that these fish are very much live organisms. They live, breathe, feed, and die just as other fish do, you just might have trouble distinguishing…any of their behaviors. Their lifestyle can be best compared to that of a starfish, lying dormant at the bed of the waters, feeding off of anything that happens to land into its permanently open mouth. As such, these creatures are a bit of an annoyance to catch, as they tend to cover the bottom of fishing pools and ponds, completely out of sight to fishers hoping for a rarer catch. If you're looking for a fish to get tired of catching, Taiyaki Feeders will always be waiting for your next hook.

Taiyaki pastries originally made their way to Pollywood through a tourism initiative, where F.I.S.H.E. marketers scanned the galaxy for any local fish-themed traditions that could be brought to the Intergalactic Fishbowl for an exotic touch*. These grilled treats with a sweet, filled center came from the Earth country of Japan. Unsurprisingly, Taiyaki Feeders were never spotted until market vendors started selling the pastries. Therefore, biologists hypothesize that they were originally some sort of chameleon fish species, which changed form to imitate the scenery around them (unfortunately, it seems their disguises were too good to detect earlier on, which grieves many biologists). For some reason, they chose to adopt the Taiyaki as their final form. 

*Other parts of the initiative, including Guryolan fish-shaped desktop computers and human fish kites, can be found on the Pollywood Boardwalk during tournament season.
"
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://cr3nmjdvpgh0a"
